{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789307662,"nonce":"3rAXlGlnQ10slJkV1wopYa4qQLE=","title":"Inference: seed parameter types from #export, and record expression-body results","message":"caribou reads a member's `#export = \"add(n: Num) -\u003e Num\"` attribute for\nthe types it exposes, and takes a result the inferrer already knows\n(sema::types::infer_types_with_classes) when the attribute leaves it\nout. Two things the inferrer could do that would let most annotations\ngo:\n\n1. Seed a parameter's type from the method's `#export` attribute, so\n   `_score = score` in a constructor annotated `new(score: Num)` types\n   the field, and the getters and methods built on it follow.\n2. Record a one-expression body (`score { _score }`, parsed as\n   Stmt::Expr) as the method's result, as a `return` is; today only\n   Stmt::Return reaches record_method_return_type, and a caller has to\n   read the expression's type itself.\n\nA third, larger: write what inference concludes into the MIR as\nattributes, so the running class carries the types too and\ncaribou_wren::publish_module answers the same as `--describe`.","files":null}]}